/F1 18 Tf 72 720 Td (Chapter 1: Hollin Point Light) Tj T* T*
/F1 11 Tf
(Hollin Point Light was the first lighthouse in the bay, completed in 1823. It stands) Tj T*
(31 metres tall and is built from grey granite quarried at Tarrow Hill. Its light) Tj T*
(flashes white twice every ten seconds and is visible for 18 nautical miles. The first) Tj T*
(keeper was Tobias Wren, who kept the light for 42 years and recorded every storm in a) Tj T*
(leather logbook that is now displayed in the bay museum. During the great gale of) Tj T*
(1852 Wren rowed out alone and rescued eleven sailors from the brig Seraphine after it) Tj T*
(struck the Hollin Reef.) Tj T*
ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 296 40 Td (Page 2) Tj ET
