/F1 18 Tf 72 720 Td (Chapter 4: Southreach Light) Tj T* T*
/F1 11 Tf
(Southreach Light guards the southern entrance to the bay. Finished in 1902, it is the) Tj T*
(tallest of the five at 44 metres, and its octagonal tower is made of brick covered in) Tj T*
(white render. The light uses a rotating first-order Fresnel lens that weighs nearly) Tj T*
(six tonnes and floats on a bath of mercury so that it turns smoothly. It shows a) Tj T*
(white flash every fifteen seconds. Southreach also had a fog signal: a compressed-air) Tj T*
(horn nicknamed the Old Bull, which sounded two long blasts every minute in poor) Tj T*
(visibility until it was retired in 1987.) Tj T*
ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 296 40 Td (Page 5) Tj ET
endstream
