16 TL
/F1 18 Tf 72 720 Td (Chapter 5: Automation and the Bay Today) Tj T* T*
/F1 11 Tf
(All five lighthouses were automated between 1979 and 1994. Hollin Point was the last) Tj T*
(to lose its keepers, on 30 June 1994. The lights are now monitored remotely from a) Tj T*
(control room in the town of Saltmere, and solar panels power the Marrowind Lantern) Tj T*
(and Cassel Rock Light. The Merrow Bay Lighthouse Trust maintains the keepers') Tj T*
(cottages and runs guided walks along the 23-kilometre coastal path that links the) Tj T*
(four mainland lights. Tickets for the boat trip to Cassel Rock must be booked in) Tj T*
(advance because landings depend on the tide.) Tj T*
ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 296 40 Td (Page 6) Tj ET
